From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tom Plant <tom@tplant.com.au>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 06:40:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] mmc: sdhci-of-dwcmshc: force card detect for non-removable
 TH1520 slots

The TH1520 SDIO controller on the Lichee Pi 4A has no card-detect
signal, so PRESENT_STATE reports no card (0x03fa0000) and CMD5 to the
RTL8723DS times out with -110. Set the card-detect test level to
"inserted" after each reset when the slot is non-removable.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
--- a/drivers/mmc/host/sdhci-of-dwcmshc.c
+++ b/drivers/mmc/host/sdhci-of-dwcmshc.c
@@ -1041,9 +1041,22 @@
 	struct sdhci_pltfm_host *pltfm_host = sdhci_priv(host);
 	struct dwcmshc_priv *priv = sdhci_pltfm_priv(pltfm_host);
 	u16 ctrl_2;
+	u8 ctrl;
 
 	dwcmshc_reset(host, mask);
 
+	/*
+	 * The card-detect input of a controller wired to a non-removable
+	 * device (the Lichee Pi 4A SDIO Wi-Fi) is not connected, so the
+	 * controller reports no card and does not drive the SD bus. Force
+	 * the card-detect test level to "inserted".
+	 */
+	if (host->mmc->caps & MMC_CAP_NONREMOVABLE) {
+		ctrl = sdhci_readb(host, SDHCI_HOST_CONTROL);
+		ctrl |= SDHCI_CTRL_CDTEST_INS | SDHCI_CTRL_CDTEST_EN;
+		sdhci_writeb(host, ctrl, SDHCI_HOST_CONTROL);
+	}
+
 	if (priv->flags & FLAG_IO_FIXED_1V8) {
 		ctrl_2 = sdhci_readw(host, SDHCI_HOST_CONTROL2);
 		if (!(ctrl_2 & SDHCI_CTRL_VDD_180)) {
